    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Sylvia Kilver, daughter of a Yale Egyptologist, was Embraced by the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.jaYCq9rVOh0I9NCN]{Tremere} in 1923 after her expertise in Egyptian antiquities and black-market dealings caught the eye of a secret Tremere order devoted to serpent worship. Sent to Cairo's new museum chantry under regent Kasper von Aupfholme, she chafed under his dismissive treatment and struck out on her own, falling into a dangerous partnership with the Setite sorceress Kahina &mdash; trading mummified relics and Tremere secrets for lessons in the Setite blood magic called Akhu.</p><p>Sylvia's price has escalated steadily: from antiquities to favors to clan secrets, and finally to swallowing a living Egyptian asp at Kahina's command to advance in the secret Setite-aligned order she serves. In exchange she developed her own Thaumaturgical path, Soul of the Serpent, which she believes to be entirely her own achievement. With von Aupfholme missing in the Western Desert pursuing the Shenouda Cache, Sylvia now serves as acting regent and eagerly awaits confirmation of his permanent disappearance so she may claim the chantry outright.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Size up everyone you meet as a potential asset or threat, projecting effortless authority over Tremere colleagues you privately despise. Around @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.ssX4b2JFXF2uegC3]{Followers of Set}, however, drop the mask entirely into genuine, unsettling deference.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Ophelia (Hartford chantry). Secretly compromised by the Setite sorceress Kahina, who has informed her that Kasper von Aupfholme will not return, clearing Sylvia's path to the regency. Developed the Thaumaturgical path Soul of the Serpent (Serpentine Sense, Scaleskin, Venom Curse, Touch of Typhon, Form of the Hydra) as a direct result of her Setite corruption; see the disciplines compendium for these powers as Thaumaturgy (Soul of the Serpent) items.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
